# Cursor Project Rules for TaskMaster SaaS
## AI-Driven Development
- 100% AI‑Generated Code: All code, tests, and deployment scripts must be generated by the AI assistant.
- Self‑Verifying: AI provides unit, integration, and end‑to‑end tests for every feature.

## Real‑World Deployment & Security
- OWASP Top 10 compliance: input validation, secure headers, CSRF/XSS protection.
- Automated Audits: Run ESLint, Prettier, SonarQube, Snyk, npm audit before deploy.
- Penetration Testing: Include scripts/instructions for automated pentests.
- Secret Management: Use vaults (HashiCorp, AWS Secrets Manager) or env vars; never commit secrets.

## General Rules
- Do not modify the tech stack specified in tech_stack_document.mdc.
- Follow the folder structure defined in backend_structure_document.mdc.
- Use Tailwind CSS exclusively for styling, as per frontend_guidelines_document.mdc.
- Do not add features outside the scope defined in project_requirements_document.mdc.
- Maintain the anime/Ghibli theme:
  - Define font-anime in tailwind.config.js under theme.extend.fontFamily.
  - Import the custom font via @font-face in src/index.css.

## Code Execution
- Execute each step in implementation_plan_document.mdc sequentially.
- If an error occurs, log the error and stop execution, providing a detailed error message.
- Do not assume missing information; if a step is unclear, prompt for clarification.

## Security Rules
- Sanitize all user inputs before processing (e.g., task title, description).
- Ensure all API requests include Clerk JWT tokens for authentication.
- Do not expose sensitive data (e.g., database connection strings) in logs or responses.

## Performance Rules
- Optimize API responses to return only necessary data (e.g., avoid over-fetching task fields).
- Ensure frontend components re-render only when necessary (use React.memo where applicable).
- Limit database queries to fetch only the required data (e.g., use Mongoose’s select).

## Documentation Integration
- Refer to app_flow_document.mdc for user journey and edge cases.
- Use frontend_guidelines_document.mdc for component structure and styling.
- Use backend_structure_document.mdc for API endpoint implementation.